[h2]Round-Based Team Deathmatch[/h2]
Two teams of up to eight fight elimination rounds. During warmup, players can mark themselves ready and vote for the match arena when the lobby leaves a choice. At the start of every round, choose equipment in the Virtual Arsenal. Once you are eliminated, you spectate until the next round.

[list]
[*]Play a fixed arena, one random arena or alternating arenas. Alternating arenas change during the match, and each is played from both spawns.
[*]With restricted loadouts, better equipment unlocks as the match progresses. The host can also allow unrestricted loadouts. Set the warmup and equipment-phase durations separately.
[*]Set when the zone starts shrinking, how fast it shrinks and how much damage it deals outside. The host can also disable shrinking or set a round time limit.
[*]Optional vehicles: choose quad bikes, sport hatchbacks, Ifrits, Hunters or Striders. Allocate vehicles per team, per two players or per player.
[*]Choose a best-of format and whether a two-point lead is required. Fill with AI to balance teams, match the arena size or reach a fixed team size.
[*]Choose whether eliminated players can spectate their own team or everyone.
[/list]

The lobby also controls arena size, AI skill, automatic healing, weather, start time, night skip, time multipliers and third-person view. The mission includes map and 3D icons, Killfeed, Dynamic Weather, Earplugs, Jump, Holster, Unflip, Magazine Repack, Disable Stamina and Disable Tactical View. Press [b]F4[/b] for view distance and icon settings.

[h2]Start the scenario[/h2]
Host the scenario in multiplayer and open Parameters in the lobby.

